---
/** Explore the app page body: the one iframe with the Desktop / Phone control, instructions, persona sign-in chips, mobile note. */
import { APP_SIGN_IN } from '../lib/links';
import TagChip from './TagChip.astro';
import DemoFrame from './DemoFrame.astro';
const people = ['Priya', 'Sam', 'Harriet', 'Nadia'];
---
<section data-section="explorer" aria-labelledby="ex-h" class="border-b border-rule">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-wrap px-5 sm:px-8 pt-10 pb-8 grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,5fr)_minmax(0,7fr)] lg:items-end">
    <div>
      <TagChip label="Explore the app" />
      <h1 id="ex-h" class="mt-4 text-4xl sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl leading-[0.98] tracking-[-0.02em]">Explore the app</h1>
    </div>
    <div class="text-[17px] leading-[1.5]">
      <p>Pick a person to see the demo as they would. Priya runs operations across two centres. Sam is a contractor and sees only his assets. Harriet sees all five sites, including Wattleford Central and Brindle Park.</p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-ink-2 text-[15px]">A working demo with a fictional portfolio, Harbourline Property, and five invented sites: Ridgeway Fair, Marlow Central, Quay Tower, Wattleford Central and Brindle Park. Two of them, Wattleford Central and Brindle Park, are drawn on layouts derived from real centres in OpenStreetMap, with invented names and data. Nothing in the demo belongs to a real property group.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-wrap px-5 sm:px-8 pb-12">
    <DemoFrame variant="explore" />
    <p class="mt-3 text-[13px] leading-[18px] text-ink-2 md:hidden">On a phone, <a href={APP_SIGN_IN} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="underline underline-offset-4 text-ink">open the demo in its own tab</a>; it installs to your home screen.</p>
  </div>
</section>
<section data-section="quick-links" aria-labelledby="ql-h" class="bg-card border-b border-rule">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-wrap px-5 sm:px-8 py-10 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-8 gap-y-4">
    <p id="ql-h" class="text-[17px] leading-[1.5] text-ink-2 max-w-[34rem]">The sign-in page above lists the people in the demo. Open it in its own tab as any of them; on a phone, it installs to your home screen.</p>
    <ul class="flex flex-wrap gap-2" aria-label="Sign in to the demo as">
      {people.map((p) => (
        <li><a href={APP_SIGN_IN} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="tag tag-lg hover:bg-ink-raised"><span class="sr-only">Sign in as </span>{p}</a></li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
